  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1000,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Scope and freshness",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Freshness rule: a current target is `up == 1` with sample age at most 90s. Missing or stale samples are unknown, never healthy and never zero. `up` is scrape availability only, not backend health.\n\n**Partial scope (owner ratified).** S3 request rate and latency are bucketless only; volume counts are default-collection only; neither is a global aggregate. `max_volumes` is a count, not capacity. No physical disk occupancy and no per-bucket or per-collection panels. PVC and PV capacity is declared or requested size from KSM, not actual usage."
      }
    },
    {
